                <pb facs="0859" n="1817" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1817"/>

                <head>No. 61.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Garland to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Justice</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-11-14"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 14, 1888</date>.
                        (Received November 16.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your communication of the 27th ultimo, concerning the disposition of the British
                    vessels now lying at Port Townsend, Wash., and to inform you that T. J.
                    Hamilton, deputy United States marshal in charge, has this day been directed to
                    take the necessary steps to effect the sale of the four vessels as speedily as
                    possible.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. H. Garland.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
